# Global machine instructions

## Dotfile management

This account manages user configuration with chezmoi.

- Active chezmoi source: `{{ .chezmoi.sourceDir }}`.
- The historical `~/dotfiles` checkout is not the active source; do not edit it.
- `~/.dotfiles` contains migration notes and TODO documentation, not deployed
  configuration.
- Before changing a dotfile or configuration under `$HOME`, check whether
  chezmoi manages it with `chezmoi managed --path-style absolute` and inspect
  any drift with `chezmoi diff -- <target>`.
- Never edit a managed destination such as `~/.zshrc` or `~/.config/...`
  directly. Edit the corresponding file under `{{ .chezmoi.sourceDir }}`.
- If a managed destination already has an external/manual change, preserve it:
  review the diff and merge the desired change into the source before applying.
  Do not overwrite it blindly.
- For a new user configuration file that should persist, use `chezmoi add
  <target>` (with appropriate template, private, or encryption attributes)
  rather than leaving an unmanaged file.
- Preview changes with a targeted `chezmoi diff`, apply with a targeted
  `chezmoi apply`, validate the affected program, and confirm `chezmoi status`
  afterward.
- Commit changes from the chezmoi source repository. Pushing over SSH may
  require a physical YubiKey touch.
- Never commit credentials or secret-bearing runtime files. In particular,
  Pi authentication and session files and GNOME Keyring data are not dotfiles.
- Project-owned files inside normal code repositories are edited normally;
  this chezmoi workflow applies to account/machine configuration, not every
  file under `$HOME`.

{{ if eq .chezmoi.hostname "terra" -}}
## Terra-specific policy

- This host runs Arch Linux with Sway.
- Curated top-level package manifests live in
  `~/.config/pkglist/{system,desktop,tools}.txt`. When deliberately installing
  or removing Arch packages, update the appropriate managed manifest.
- `/etc` is not managed by chezmoi. Treat system configuration changes as
  explicit administrative work, inspect first, and create a backup when
  appropriate.
- Current migration notes and deferred work are in
  `~/.dotfiles/migration.md` and `~/.dotfiles/todo.md`.
{{ end -}}
